# The observing run works without this. A fine-grained, read-only token with
# public-repository access raises the GitHub rate limit from 60 requests an
# hour to 5,000, and the panel states which mode it ran in either way.
#
# Never a classic token, never write scope: this survey reads public metadata.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Where the run caches responses, keyed per commit SHA. Defaults to the system
# temp directory, which is the only writable path on most serverless hosts.
# MERIDIAN_CACHE=.meridian-cache
